text:
violet: GA announcement: Hosted Mobile Streaming v1.0 + mosaic-mini-mobile model are live. Docs and migration guide published. Huge thanks to eng-runtime and devex teams! :tada:
sam: Congrats everyone! Any actionable changes for partners or SDKs?
violet: Default now uses websocket multiplexing to reduce connections and power usage. Legacy single-socket will continue for 45 days with deprecation warnings. No billing changes.
docs-bot: Published: https://docs.redwood.ai/mobile-streaming - includes quickstart, migration steps, and perf table.
violet: Perf snapshot (128 tok): p50=42ms, p90=150ms, p99=310ms on mosaic-mini w/ 8-bit quant, mobile profile. Battery/cpu improvements noted in tests.
sre-bot: Rollout plan: 5% -> 30% (12h) -> 80% (24h) -> 100% (36h). SRE will enable adaptive backpressure at 30% bump. Pager if websocket error rate >2% for 5m.
tony: JS migration example?
violet: Simple snippet:
```
import {MobileStream} from '@redwood/mobile-stream';
const client = new MobileStream({ url: 'wss://hosted.redwood.ai/mobile/v1' });
await client.connect({ model: 'mosaic-mini-v1', multiplex: true });
const s = client.stream({ prompt: 'Summarize this note', max_tokens: 128 });
s.on('delta', d => console.log(d));
s.on('end', () => console.log('done'));
```
sam: We'll update RN + Android SDKs to enable multiplex=true by default and add the deprecation warning for single-socket.
violet: Ops note: watch for connection storms during 30% rollout window. If you see retries, slow down client backoff. Reach out in #eng-oncall if issues.
tony: I'll notify top partners and schedule a 1:1 migration office hour tomorrow.
violet: Thanks all, will post a short blog + internal playbook after soak. :rocket:
